        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## FLUX.1 [dev]: img2img, ControlNet\n\nThe FLUX.1 [dev] workflow for img2img, with ControlNet. Write full\ndescriptive sentences and put literal text in quotes; there is no negative prompt (embedded guidance, not true CFG).\n\n**Settings**: 20 steps (28-30 for finals), guidance 3.5 (Distilled CFG in the Generate tab), euler, simple,\n1024×1024 or another ~1 MP size (multiples of 16). **Width** and **Height** feed **Resize to** and **ModelSamplingFlux**,\nwhose shift grows with the image size.\n\n## img2img\n\nThe image of **Load Image ib:img** is the starting point: **Resize to** scales it to the size of the Generate tab\n(Width / Height, its *Resize to* in img2img mode; **Use size** in the Input cell takes the size of the image),\n**VAE Encode** makes the latent, and the sampler adds noise by the **denoising** strength (0.6 here) and samples\nfrom there. The prompt describes the whole image you want. Low denoising keeps the composition and colors; high\ndenoising moves further from the image. To change one area only, use the inpaint workflow; to change the image by\nan instruction, an edit model with references.\n\nThe Generate tab is in **img2img** mode while this workflow is loaded. Send an image with **Send to the input\nimage** (B), from the editor, or upload it in the Input cell before the first queue. This workflow has no Hires.\nfix pass: upscale the result with the full workflow.\n\n## Image Bench\n\n| Marker | Node | Generate / ControlNet tab |\n|--------|------|---------------------------|\n| `ib:cp` | Load Diffusion Model | model list, model exploration |\n| `ib:img` | Load Image | Input cell; Send to the input image (B), the editor |\n| `ib:pp` | Image Bench Prompt | prompt and LoRA list |\n| `ib:smp` | SamplerCustomAdvanced | seed (RandomNoise), steps and scheduler (BasicScheduler), sampling method, Distilled CFG (FluxGuidance), denoising; Resize to (Width / Height) |\n| `ib:cn:0` | ControlNet Depth | ControlNet tab, unit 1 |\n| `ib:cn:1` | ControlNet Canny | ControlNet tab, unit 2 |\n| `ib:lora` | Load LoRA (bypassed) | LoRA exploration only |\n\n**ControlNet** ([Union Pro 2.0](https://huggingface.co/Shakker-Labs/FLUX.1-dev-ControlNet-Union-Pro-2.0): canny, soft\nedge, depth, pose, gray in one model, no control type to set): each unit is an **Apply ControlNet** node, bypassed\nwhile the unit is disabled; Enable in the ControlNet tab turns it on. The tab sets weight (strength) and guidance range,\nthe model, the control image (**Send to ControlNet**, a drop, or Photoshop: *ControlNet: preprocess* runs the\npreprocessor and sends the map back) and the preprocessor of its **AIO Aux Preprocessor** (Depth Anything V2 and\nCanny here; set it to *none* for a ready-made map). The model card's settings: canny 0.7 / end 0.8, soft edge\n(AnylineDetector) 0.7 / 0.8, depth 0.8 / 0.8, pose (DWPose) 0.9 / 0.65, gray 0.9 / 0.8. An end of 0.6-0.8 avoids\nplastic skin and baked-in edge lines before the strength needs lowering. Both units can run together (one model\nfile, loaded once). FLUX has no negative conditioning; **Negative for the ControlNet nodes** only fills their\nnegative input. The core apply node has no mask input, so Use Mask is not offered.\n\nPut any ESRGAN-type model into\n`models/upscale_models` ([RealESRGAN_x4plus.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Real-ESRGAN_repackaged/resolve/main/RealESRGAN_x4plus.safetensors) here).\n\n**LoRAs**: check them in the LoRA list or type `<lora:name:weight>` into the prompt.\n\nBatch generation, model and LoRA exploration, varying parameters, PNG Info, projects and the Compare tab work\nas with every marked workflow. There is no reference slot: image references need FLUX.1 Kontext [dev] or Redux.\n\n## Required custom nodes\n\n- **comfyui_controlnet_aux** for the preprocessors (without it, set the preprocessors to *none* or delete them and\n  link the control images to the apply nodes).\n\n## Model Links\n\n**diffusion_models**: [flux1-dev-fp8.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Kijai/flux-fp8/resolve/main/flux1-dev-fp8.safetensors) (Kijai, fp8 e4m3fn, 12 GB;\nthe bf16 [flux1-dev.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.1-dev) of Black Forest Labs is gated)\n**text_encoders**: [clip_l.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/comfyanonymous/flux_text_encoders/resolve/main/clip_l.safetensors),\n[t5xxl_fp16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/comfyanonymous/flux_text_encoders/resolve/main/t5xxl_fp16.safetensors)\n(or [t5xxl_fp8_e4m3fn_scaled.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/comfyanonymous/flux_text_encoders/resolve/main/t5xxl_fp8_e4m3fn_scaled.safetensors) with less memory)\n**vae**: [ae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Lumina_Image_2.0_Repackaged/resolve/main/split_files/vae/ae.safetensors)\n**controlnet**: [FLUX.1-dev-ControlNet-Union-Pro-2.0-fp8.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/ABDALLALSWAITI/FLUX.1-dev-ControlNet-Union-Pro-2.0-fp8/resolve/main/diffusion_pytorch_model.safetensors)\n(saved as `diffusion_pytorch_model.safetensors`: rename it; 2 GB, the bf16 original of\n[Shakker-Labs](https://huggingface.co/Shakker-Labs/FLUX.1-dev-ControlNet-Union-Pro-2.0) has 4 GB)\n\nFLUX.1 [dev] is under the FLUX.1 [dev] non-commercial license.\n"
      ],
      "title": "Note: FLUX.1 [dev] (Image Bench, img2img)",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
